; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- what HomerScribe is made of, and the rules its keys follow.

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=HomerScribe is one dialog. Each part is named by the narrator and then shown by the screen reader: the boxes for what to work on and where to write, the boxes that say what to do, the keys that read a field, the keys that report progress, and the four kinds of help.
Setup=HomerScribe is installed.
Homework=Open HomerScribe, Tab through every control once, and press Shift plus F1 on each to hear its tip.

[step]

Say=HomerScribe is one dialog, built the way every Homer dialog is: a label, then the control it names. I name each part; the reader shows it, as it would on your machine.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus H, H for HomerScribe, opens it from anywhere.
Key=Alt+Control+H
Hear=HomerScribe dialog
Hear=Source paths: edit, https colon slash slash www dot youtube dot com slash watch question mark v equals 3 f 31 o u f q F S M

[step]

Say=The window's name, then where focus is: Source paths, an edit box, holding the sample film's address. Here go the files, folders, wildcard patterns or web addresses to work on. Shift plus F1 reads any field's tip.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=One or more files, wildcard patterns, or web addresses to download from, separated by spaces. Put double quotes around any item containing a space.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every field has a tip, in the same words the help box uses. Alt plus F8 reads the whole field aloud, or says Blank.
Key=Alt+F8
Hear=https colon slash slash www dot youtube dot com slash watch question mark v equals 3 f 31 o u f q F S M
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Tab moves in the order the controls were added: Browse source, then the output folder, then the boxes that say what to do.
Key=Tab
Hear=Browse source... button, Alt plus B
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now the rule behind every key here: the word gives the letter. Alt plus a letter goes straight to its control, and for a check box it ticks or clears it. Alt plus T, T for Transcribe.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Transcribe audio check box, checked, Alt plus T

[step]

Say=Checked. Again, and it is cleared.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Transcribe audio check box, not checked, Alt plus T
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=D for Describe, A for Audio only, W for Web context, R for Remove ads, F for Force overwrite, L for Log session. Alt plus O goes to the Output directory box, O for Output.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Output directory: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Where the documents are written; blank means beside each source. A dialog this size has many controls, so F7 lists them all; a letter jumps to one and Enter goes to it.
Key=F7
Hear=Controls list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the list and returns where I was. In the dialog itself, Enter presses OK from anywhere, Control plus Enter from inside a box of many lines, and Escape cancels.
Key=Escape
Hear=Output directory: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=While the work runs, the dialog stays, its controls resting, and its title says what is happening. Two keys ask how it goes: Shift plus F6 says how far through the current file; Control plus Page Down and Page Up move between its stages. And Insert plus T, the reader's own key, reads the title.
Key=Insert+T
Hear=HomerScribe dialog

[step]

Say=Help is in four places, the same in every Homer program. I say which; the reader says the key. The help box, listing every field and key, and the version.
Key=
Hear=F1, the help box

[step]

Say=The tip for the field you are on.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F1

[step]

Say=A list of the controls, to reach any one.
Key=
Hear=F7

[step]

Say=And the guide and the hotkeys, as documents in the Start menu.
Key=
Hear=HomerScribe documentation

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Alt plus O is the Output box, so pressing it to accept does not press OK. I press it, and the reader shows where I landed.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Output directory: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The answer is Enter, which presses OK from anywhere. What this walk taught. I name the part; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Tick Transcribe audio.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus T

[step]

Say=Hear a field's tip.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F1

[step]

Say=Hear a whole field.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus F8

[step]

Say=Accept from anywhere.
Key=
Hear=Enter
